      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Elevated plasma leucine levels act as a primary \"stop sign\" that triggersmechanosensitive opening of mTORC1 signaling, bypassing the inhibitor SCF<sup>Fbw7</sup> and directly binding to Rag GTPases to translocate mTORC1 to the lysosome for rapid activation. Within a caloric surplus, the excess energy surplus coupled with adequate protein intake shifts nitrogen balance into a positive state, allowing the body to capture and retain free amino acids primarily as protein for muscle growth. This synergy ensures that the metabolic signals for synthesis are supported by the necessary macronutrient substrate availability to maximize hypertrophy outcomes.",
