    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Leucine facilitates the dissociation of the GTPase Rap1BP1 from mTOR, a process that normally stabilizes the inhibitor Sestrin2; by displacing this stabilizer, excess leucine allows mTORC1 to irrepressively phosphorylate downstream effectors like 4E-BP1. Regarding caloric surplus efficiency, excessive energy intakes without proportional protein increases often lead to diminishing returns, as surplus nitrogen is metabolized into energy rather than stored as muscle protein. Therefore, optimizing the surplus means prioritizing high leucine intake alongside a moderate caloric excess to ensure nitrogen retention specifically funds structural gains rather than just fat accumulation.",
